    "body": "## What\n\nFormat the merge-resolved ask and terminal files, map recoverably paused tasks to the native protocol's parked state, and move runtime VERSION/USER_AGENT constants to the native-free version utility. Migrate direct imports and document the native archive build constraint.\n\n## Why\n\nRepair the formatting/type failures and CLI bundling failure exposed after upstream v18.4.4 integration. The compiler previously loaded the native directory before generating its archive; Bun cached that directory listing and could not resolve the new archive. Upstream v18.4.3/v18.4.4 tags are now published to the fork so version derivation uses the correct release.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Full local `bun run check:ts` passed after the final changes. No local native or CLI compilation.\n- Reproduced the missing-archive failure in the Arch CI runtime with a preloaded native module, then verified successful asset bundling with the actual native-free version module.\n- Merged ahead of remote validation at the user's explicit request to prioritize the Arch build; canceled superseded/duplicate source jobs, then ran source CI #70 against merged SHA `4de24f3358686f74df84141156e38e019516e0c6`. It passed frozen installation, lint/format/types, Rust checks, web/native/CLI builds, and the exact compiled-version assertion.\n- Arch build #147 passed with source `4de24f3358686f74df84141156e38e019516e0c6`, recipe `080fbab6a028b7d70f0318622eefe1e062cd62ae`, and preserved `mesa=mesa` selection.\n- Signed package `oh-my-pi-vith-git-18.4.4.vith.r320.g4de24f335868-1-x86_64.pkg.tar.zst` and repository database are published. Both signatures verified with fingerprint `433D492D0438666BBB7230BB91D0A55E51016A94`; package SHA256 matches its database entry. The extracted packaged executable prints `omp/18.4.4+vith-fork.320.4de24f335868`. No package installation or system trust changes.\n- TS/Rust suites and worker smoke tests remain disabled under the temporary policy; checks/build success is not a test-suite pass. No new changelog entry was requested.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] `bun check` passes\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [ ] CHANGELOG updated with the required attribution (if user-facing; internal issue fixes use issue links, external contributions add the PR link and contributor credit after creation)",
    "changed_files": 14,
